Rules for the game - SLASH
.sp
.il 3
SLASH is a realtime video game meant for 3270's.  The game board is a
visual  representation of  an  area of  space in  which  bombs (#)   are
scattered randomly at the start and remain stationary for the duration of
the game or until they are destroyed, whichever comes first.
.sp
.il 3
Aside from the  bombs there is a  plane (@)  which has  the following
rules of motion:
.il 3
whenever the  plane strikes  the wall  it rebounds  by reversing  its
direction;
.il 3
whenever a plane strikes  a '\' or a '/' it changes  its course by 90
degrees;
.il 3
whenever the plane strikes a bomb, the bomb is destroyed.
.sp
.il 3
At the start  of the game there are  no SLASHes on the  board and the
plane will just fly  back and forth across the screen.    To add SLASHes
press PA1 for  '\',  or,  PA2 for '/',   and a SLASH will  appear at the
plane's  current  location  causing  the   latter  to  change  direction
immediately.   An occupied  position on the screen (one with  a SLASH in
it)  cannot be changed by placing a new  SLASH in it.   The plane may go
into a loop from which no exit is possible.
.sp
.il 3
If you find  yourself breathless you may freeze the  game by pressing
SYS-REQ, To resume the game press SYS-REQ again.   Pressing ENTER at any
point  in the  game  other  then freeze  mode  will  terminate the  game
immediately.   Due  to the  speed of the  program the  CLEAR key  is not
handled very successfully, try to refrain from using it unless CP erases
the screen in order to display a message,  in which case,  after looking
at the message, you should press CLEAR or PA2.
.sp
.of 8
NOTICE: If the game "hangs up" at some point press SYS-REQ to resume the
game.
.of
.sp
.il 3
When the game is  invoked you may specify how many  bombs you want (1
to 100) as the first parameter to the program.  The score isn't adjusted
accordingly,  so try to use the default (30).   The score of the game is
calculated as follows:
.sp
.fo off
.in 3
   4 points awarded for every bomb destroyed;
   1 point deducted for every 60 "seconds" of game time;
   1 point deducted for every SLASH used.
.in
.fo on
.sp
.il 3
When all  the bombs have  been destroyed the  game will stop  and the
final screen will stay put until you  cause an interrupt with any of the
ENTER, PFs, PAs etc.. keys.
.sp
.il 3
The game SLASH will  work on any 3277 or 3278  device and will adjust
itself to the maximum display area on the given device.
.sp
.fo off
   Written for your enjoyment by: Yossie Silverman, W.I.C.C, Israel.
.fo on
